paragraphs.en:
The wind whispers in my ear,
shaking my coat-tails, saying not to stand still for even a step;
the skylark, like a young lady beyond the fence, laughs a greeting from behind the clouds.

Butterflies and swallows, do not flit about in such haste;
I must greet the dandelions and the violets too.
The field where a woman with castor oil in her hair used to weed: I want to see it all.

